  "notes": "The completion of a financial transaction. A compound of {決|けつ} (settle) + {済|さい} (finish). More formal and technical than ⟦{支払|しはら}い→支払い：03193_shiharai⟧ (payment).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {決済|けっさい}⟦{方法|ほうほう}→方法：03621_houhou⟧: payment method\n- ⟦{電子|でんし}→電子：03449_denshi⟧{決済|けっさい}: electronic payment\n- ⟦キャッシュレス→キャッシュレス：06096_kyasshuresu⟧{決済|けっさい}: cashless payment\n- {決済|けっさい}⟦{完了|かんりょう}→完了：02560_kanryou⟧: payment completed\n- {決済|けっさい}する: to complete a payment\n\nMODERN USAGE:\nVery common in e-commerce, fintech, and POS systems. ⟦QRコード→QRコード：06403_kyuuaarukoodo⟧{決済|けっさい} (QR code payment) has become widespread in Japan.\n\nWATCH OUT:\n⟦{決裁|けっさい}→決裁：11100_kessai⟧ means \"approval/authorization\" (different kanji, different meaning).",
